body:
### Tested versions

Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.steam [49a5bc7b6]

### System information

Godot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 580 2048SP (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21923.11000) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600G with Radeon Graphics (12 threads)

### Issue description

When exposing a typed dictionary in the editor with C++ GDextension, trying to access it in any way via GDScript will cause the following error, even when the dictionary is provided with said information.

<img width="832" height="328" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd5dcc25-9ccb-4f2d-811b-52daa448bd1d" />


Error:
E 0:00:01:279   type_from_property: Could not find element type from property hint of a typed dictionary.
  <C++ Error>   Method/function failed. Returning: result
  <C++ Source>  modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp:5623 @ type_from_property()

[Link](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/49a5bc7b616bd04689a2c89e89bda41f50241464/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L5623)

### Steps to reproduce

Create a typed dictionary with its corresponding getter, setter and property. Then try to access it through GDScript.

.h
```c++
class ProjectileBlueprint2D: public Resource {
	GDCLASS(ProjectileBlueprint2D, Resource);

	public:
		void set_global_properties(TypedDictionary<StringName, Variant> dictionary);
		TypedDictionary<StringName, Variant> get_global_properties() const;

	protected:
		static void _bind_methods();

	private:
		TypedDictionary<StringName, Variant> global_properties;
};
```

.cpp
```c++
void ProjectileBlueprint2D::set_global_properties(TypedDictionary<StringName, Variant> dictionary){
	global_properties = dictionary; 
}
TypedDictionary<StringName, Variant> ProjectileBlueprint2D::get_global_properties() const {
	return global_properties;
}

void ProjectileBlueprint2D::_bind_methods(){
	ClassDB::bind_method(D_METHOD("set_global_properties", "dictionary"), &ProjectileBlueprint2D::set_global_properties);
	ClassDB::bind_method(D_METHOD("get_global_properties"), &ProjectileBlueprint2D::get_global_properties);
	ADD_PROPERTY(PropertyInfo(Variant::DICTIONARY, "global_properties", PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING, 
		String::num(Variant::STRING_NAME) + ":;" + String::num(Variant::NIL) + ":"), "set_global_properties", "get_global_properties");
}
```

test.gd
```gdscript
@export var proj_blueprint: ProjectileBlueprint2D

func _ready() -> void:
	proj_blueprint.global_properties
```

